try></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IDEMITSU PETROCHEMICAL CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOMOTSU, NORIO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSUJITA, YOSHIHARU</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TOMOTSU NORIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TSUJITA YOSHIHARU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOMOTSU, NORIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSUJITA, YOSHIHARU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>(1) An adsorbent made of a styrene polymer, characterized by being produced by dissolving a mainly syndiotactic styrene polymer in an organic compound having an affinity for the polymer, subjecting the obtained solution to molding, and removing the organic compound from the resulting molded article, (2) an adsorbent as set forth in the item (1) wherein the molding is conducted by melt casting, and (3) an adsorbent as set forth in the item (1) or (2) wherein the removal of the organic compound is conducted by vaporization under a reduced pressure.  These adsorbents can selectively and efficiently adsorb organic compounds contained in gases or liquids.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne (1) un adsorbant issu d'un polymère de styrène caractérisé en ce qu'il est obtenu par dissolution d'un polymère de styrène essentiellement syndiotactique dans un composé organique ayant une affinité pour ce polymère. La solution est moulée et le composé organique est extrait de l'article moulé obtenu, puis (2) l'adsorbant obtenu sous (1) est moulé par fusion et (3) le composé organique est éliminé par vaporisation sous une pression réduite. Ces adsorbants peuvent adsorber de manière efficace et sélective les composés organiques contenus dans les gaz ou liquides.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>